  "final_output": "Here is the step-by-step calculation for the approximate monthly EMI for a ₹5,00,000 loan at a 10% annual interest rate for 3 years using the standard reducing-balance EMI formula:\n\n### **Formula:**\n\\[\nEMI = P \\times \\frac{r(1 + r)^n}{(1 + r)^n - 1}\n\\]\nWhere:\n- \\(P = ₹5,00,000\\) (loan principal)\n- \\(r = \\frac{10\\%}{12} = 0.8333\\% \\approx 0.008333\\) (monthly interest rate)\n- \\(n = 3 \\times 12 = 36\\) (total number of monthly installments)\n\n### **Step-by-Step Calculation:**\n1. **Monthly interest rate (\\(r\\)):**\n   \\(r = \\frac{10\\%}{12} = 0.008333\\)\n\n2. **Total number of installments (\\(n\\)):**\n   \\(n = 3 \\times 12 = 36\\)\n\n3. **Calculate \\((1 + r)^n\\):**\n   \\((1 + 0.008333)^{36} \\approx 1.3482\\)\n\n4. **Calculate the numerator:**\n   \\(r(1 + r)^n = 0.008333 \\times 1.3482 \\approx 0.011235\\)\n\n5. **Calculate the denominator:**\n   \\((1 + r)^n - 1 = 1.3482 - 1 = 0.3482\\)\n\n6. **Calculate EMI:**\n   \\(EMI = 5,00,000 \\times \\frac{0.011235}{0.3482} \\approx ₹15,890\\)\n\n### **Results:**\n- **Approximate Monthly EMI:** **₹15,890**\n- **Total Amount Paid Over 3 Years:**\n  \\(₹15,890 \\times 36 \\approx ₹5,71,240\\)\n\n### **Summary:**\n- **Monthly EMI:** ₹15,890 (approximate)\n- **Total Repayment:** ₹5,71,240 (approximate)"
